SUMMARY:FORAGER
LOCATION:Stone Church\, 210 Main St\, Brattleboro\, VT 05301
DESCRIPTION:FORAGER is a Brooklyn-based trio whose music augments contempor
 ary indie rock with intricate guitar work\, melismatic vocals\, and curiou
 s\, shapeshifting grooves. NPR's Bobby Carter called their music "buttery"
  and "complex\," remarking\, "where have you been all my life?!?" FORAGER 
 has built their following on the strength of their live show\, selling out
  venues in New York and throughout the U.S. Their sophomore album\, Even a
  Child Can Cover the Sun with a Finger\, ventures into rawer territory—w
 hispered vocals over blaring sirens and distorted drums\, singable psych-p
 op choruses that disintegrate into mayhem. The album captures the peeled-b
 ack intimacy of folk-singer-songwriters with the pulsating synchronicity t
 hat only comes from a band.\nhttps://tickets.venuepilot.com/e/forager-2026
 -12-04-stone-church-brattleboro-3ea783\nFrom Pushpin Western Mass: https:/
 /pushpin.city/westernma/
URL:https://tickets.venuepilot.com/e/forager-2026-12-04-stone-church-brattl
 eboro-3ea783
