SUMMARY:Whores.
LOCATION:Stone Church\, 210 Main St\, Brattleboro\, VT 05301
DESCRIPTION:Tree\nFormed in 2010 in Atlanta\, Georgia\, WHORES. has establi
 shed themselves as one of the most successful and motivated bands in the n
 oise-rock genre today. Elements of Helmet\, Melvins\, and the Amphetamine 
 Reptile roster can be heard throughout their catalog\, but Whores. are no 
 regurgitated throwback act. Through intense\, cathartic live performances 
 and the perfected aggressive tenacity present on their recordings\, the ba
 nd has gained a fervent following sure to do nothing but grow in the years
  to come TREE was formed in 1986 as a punk hardcore band in Westwood Massa
 chusetts. The band played the club scene through the 80's and 90's in and 
 around Boston and New England gaining popularity. Tree\, always known to a
 dvocate for political and social justice\, came to partner with MasCann ( 
 and help spearhead the legalization movement in Massachusetts. Tree and Sa
 m Black Church would be known to alternate headlining spots at the annual 
 "Freedom Rally" on the Boston Commons\, playing to extensive audiences of 
 100k+\, and advocating for legalization. Tree's song "God Grows Grass" bec
 ame the anthem for the movement.\nhttps://tickets.venuepilot.com/e/whores-
 2026-12-12-stone-church-brattleboro-30403e\nFrom Pushpin Western Mass: htt
 ps://pushpin.city/westernma/
URL:https://tickets.venuepilot.com/e/whores-2026-12-12-stone-church-brattle
 boro-30403e
END:VEVENT
