SUMMARY:Hans Williams
LOCATION:Stone Church\, 210 Main St\, Brattleboro\, VT 05301
DESCRIPTION:New Orleans-based singer-songwriter Hans Williams makes soulful
 \, dreamy folk shaped by the people and places closest to him. His debut a
 lbum\, Songs for the Neighbors\, was born in the backyard of his Bayou St.
  John home\, where late-night jams and intimate shows regularly spill over
  fences and through open windows. Recorded largely live at the house with 
 his longtime band and producer Phin Choukas (Noah Kahan)\, the record blen
 ds folk with touches of soul\, funk\, psychedelia\, and country. At its he
 art\, Songs for the Neighbors is about connection with friends\, lovers\, 
 family\, neighbors\, and those no longer here. Warm\, intimate\, and deepl
 y human\, the album captures the feeling of people making music together a
 nd Williams’ belief that even the smallest act of reaching out can bring
  us closer. Now\, Williams is excited to bring Songs for the Neighbors out
  of the backyard and onto the stage. To play these songs live\, see famili
 ar faces\, meet new ones\, and share the record with the people who have b
 een listening along the way.\nhttps://tickets.venuepilot.com/e/hans-willia
 ms-2027-01-31-stone-church-brattleboro-8159d1\nFrom Pushpin Western Mass: 
 https://pushpin.city/westernma/
URL:https://tickets.venuepilot.com/e/hans-williams-2027-01-31-stone-church-
 brattleboro-8159d1
END:VEVENT
